{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.departure_factor_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.departure_factor_eq","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CrossingWeightAffine.lean#L132-L138","doc":"**Departure prefactor = Q_β decay-numerator factor.** With `h = q − q⁻¹`,\nthe fixed scaling `(h−2)/2` equals `(q² − 2q − 1)/(2q)` — the same\n`q² − 2q − 1` factor carried by `Q_β` itself. So the crossing weight departs\nfrom the topological loop `w = 1` along the Q_β decay-numerator direction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.ladder_departure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.ladder_departure","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CrossingWeightAffine.lean#L123-L130","doc":"**Departure inversion.** The crossing weight is the counit value `1` minus\nthe ladder tail `(L − 1)` scaled by `(h−2)/2`. Machine form of\n`w − 1 = −(h−2)/2·Σ_{k≥2} c_k u^k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.ladder_counit_ref","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.ladder_counit_ref","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CrossingWeightAffine.lean#L104-L113","doc":"**`c₂ = −1` reference identity.** At the counit reference `w₀ = 1`, the\nladder factor minus one is `−2·(w − 1)/(h − 2)` — the fixed anchor-free\nmap from the crossing-weight departure `(w − 1)` into the ladder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.ladder_even_part","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.ladder_even_part","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CrossingWeightAffine.lean#L93-L102","doc":"**Ladder-factor even part.** The bar-even (shadow/mass) part of `L(w)` is\n`(4·w·w₀ − h²)/(4w₀² − h²)` — bar-even, carrying the shadow. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.ladder_odd_part","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.ladder_odd_part","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CrossingWeightAffine.lean#L80-L91","doc":"**Ladder-factor odd part.** With the reference weight `w₀`, the bar-odd\n(decay/swing) part of `L(w) = E(w)/E(w₀)` is exactly the fixed bar-odd\nkernel `2h/(4w₀² − h²)` times the crossing-weight departure `(w − w₀)`:\nLINEAR in `(w − w₀)`, no self-interaction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.evalMapBar_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.evalMapBar_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CrossingWeightAffine.lean#L68-L78","doc":"Bar image `L̄(w) = E₋(w)/E₋(w₀) = (h + 2w)/(h + 2w₀)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.evalMap_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.evalMap_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CrossingWeightAffine.lean#L59-L66","doc":"**Ladder factor in lowest terms.** Multiplying `E(w)/E(w₀)` top and bottom\nby `2/h` (`h ≠ 0`) collapses the `h²/2` to the clean fractional-linear\n(Möbius) form `L(w) = (h − 2w)/(h − 2w₀)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.evalMap_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.evalMap_affine","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CrossingWeightAffine.lean#L43-L48","doc":"**Affine in the crossing weight.** The evaluation map differs only by the\nlinear term `−h·(w − w₀)`; in particular it introduces no nonlinearity in\n`w` (`∂E/∂w = −h` is constant). Unconditional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.evalMapBar_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.evalMapBar_eq","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CrossingWeightAffine.lean#L40-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.evalMapBar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.evalMapBar","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CrossingWeightAffine.lean#L37-L38","doc":"Its bar image (`h ↦ −h`, `w` fixed): `E₋(w) = h²/2 + h·w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.evalMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine.evalMap","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CrossingWeightAffine.lean#L32-L35","doc":"The Q_β evaluation map on the `N=0` nucleon NF difference, as a function of\nthe crossing weight `w`: `E(w) = h²/2 − h·w` (`w = 1` → counit `ε`,\n`w = z` → Markov trace `tr_M`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}